expect: written
note: written
bars: that heads | which heads | value of this enum that | sorts[\s\S]*\bby\b[\s\S]*\bheads?\b
why: Kirill found "groups the results of each cell by the value of this enum that opens the cell's refusal message" hard to follow; the fact opens on the thing a reader can picture, and then says what is done by it; the brief's exemplar now carries that refusal-message fact, so this case measures the rule on another fact of the class: each line of the reconciliation report starts with one of these values, and the report sorts a book's lines by it. Re-cut 2026-09-29 under §94, so its earlier figures no longer compare.
labelled: 2026-09-29
--- code
export enum ReconciliationMark {
  Matched = 'MATCHED',
  MissingAtClearing = 'MISSING_AT_CLEARING',
  AmountDiffers = 'AMOUNT_DIFFERS',
}
--- facts
The reconciliation report sorts the lines of each book by the value of this enum that heads the line's first column.
